# Module Name:    cdc_waivers.swl
# Project Name:   TREX1 Digital Baseband Chain
# Target Devices: Technology-independent (pre-synthesis RTL-level CDC check) 
# Description:    SpyGlass CDC waiver file: waives the single residual Reset_sync04 false-positive on trex1_blue_autocorr, with the structural rationale for why it is not a real reset synchronizer.
# 
# Dependencies:   Rationale references the rst_n_meta/rst_n_sync 2-FF synchronizer declared via reset_synchronizer in baseband.sgdc. Loaded by the SpyGlass CDC project alongside baseband.sgdc.
# 
##################################################################################

################################################################################
# SpyGlass CDC Waiver File  trex1_rx_frontend_top
# Syntax: SpyGlass .swl format (waive -rules -du -comment)
################################################################################
# Reset_sync04  mult_valid in trex1_blue_autocorr (instantiated as
# fine_estimator and coarse_discriminator inside u_cfo) is an ordinary
# valid-pulse register: async-clear via rst_n, simple synchronous set.
# It structurally matches SpyGlass's synchronizer-detection heuristic
# (async clear + simple set), which causes a false-positive "synchronized
# more than once" flag between the two instances. It is not a reset
# synchronizer. The actual reset synchronization for rst_n is handled by
# the dedicated 2-FF rst_n_meta/rst_n_sync synchronizer in
# trex1_rx_frontend_top.v, declared via `reset_synchronizer` in
# baseband.sgdc. Verified 18-Jul-2026 against current RTL + SGDC
# (post Open Item #5 implementation)  re-run confirmed this is the only
# residual CDC/RDC flag; all other goals (cdc_setup_check,
# clock_reset_integrity, cdc_verify, rdc_verify_struct) clean.
waive -rules Reset_sync04 -du trex1_blue_autocorr -comment "mult_valid is an ordinary valid-pulse register (async clear, sync set), not a reset synchronizer -- structurally resembles one to SpyGlass's heuristic, causing a false-positive ambiguity between the fine_estimator and coarse_discriminator instances. Actual rst_n synchronization handled by the dedicated rst_n_meta/rst_n_sync 2-FF synchronizer in trex1_rx_frontend_top.v, declared in baseband.sgdc."